open_issues.body:
Skill loading currently parses/reads attacker- or user-controlled bundle content without complete pre-allocation bounds. Recursive directory walking can exhaust stack/entries; YAML/frontmatter and Markdown may be read fully before limits are applied; special files can block.

Required in Go and Rust:
- cap control-file/frontmatter size before parsing;
- iterative traversal with maximum depth and entry count;
- cap aggregate bytes before reading/allocating;
- reject non-regular files;
- preserve deterministic ordering and stable diagnostics;
- add deep-tree, huge-file, FIFO/special-file and boundary regressions.

Keep SKL-001 fixture-ready until the corrected contracts match.
